WEBVTT

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:03.063 --> 01:04.647
-Seok-ryu.
-Hey, right now…

01:04.731 --> 01:06.107
Hear me out first.

01:08.818 --> 01:10.820
I won't delay it any longer.

01:11.571 --> 01:13.239
I said I'd wait until later,

01:14.616 --> 01:17.535
but that was an excuse I made
to pretend to be considerate.

01:18.995 --> 01:20.538
I lied to myself.

01:22.665 --> 01:25.085
It was out of fear. I was scared.

01:28.463 --> 01:29.506
So…

01:31.341 --> 01:32.675
The thing is…

01:35.720 --> 01:37.388
I'm going to say it this time.

01:38.932 --> 01:40.975
When I said you were driving me crazy…

01:42.727 --> 01:45.104
When I said I was losing my mind
because of you…

01:46.439 --> 01:47.857
What I meant by that was…

01:50.527 --> 01:51.528
I…

01:57.867 --> 01:58.952
like you.

02:17.053 --> 02:18.221
That's hot!

02:18.847 --> 02:19.806
Hey!

02:19.889 --> 02:20.849
Are you okay?

02:21.891 --> 02:23.518
-Yeah, I'm fine.
-Let me see.

02:23.601 --> 02:24.644
No, I'm okay.

02:24.727 --> 02:26.896
-You burned yourself.
-No, I'm fine.

02:26.980 --> 02:28.481
You're going to form blisters.

02:35.321 --> 02:36.406
You should've been careful!

02:36.489 --> 02:38.950
You made it so I couldn't be careful.

02:39.033 --> 02:41.327
I didn't know you had water boiling.
I was burning inside.

02:41.411 --> 02:42.245
What are you saying?

02:42.328 --> 02:44.747
Stop moving.
We have to run cold water over this.

02:56.009 --> 03:00.013
Hey, why are your hands so warm?

03:00.096 --> 03:00.972
What?

03:02.557 --> 03:04.809
My body usually gives off a lot of heat.

03:05.602 --> 03:08.771
-Should we go to the hospital?
-No way. It's fine.

03:13.151 --> 03:15.737
Your hands are already a mess.
What if they're scarred too?

03:16.279 --> 03:17.405
It's not a big deal.

03:18.448 --> 03:20.992
I'm sure this will be
a daily occurrence now.

03:21.075 --> 03:22.702
Now that I've decided to cook,

03:22.785 --> 03:25.747
I'll get burned and cut
while battling water, fire, and oil.

03:25.830 --> 03:28.625
Jeez. I can't even tell you
to stop either.

03:28.708 --> 03:31.127
Who are you to tell me what to do?

03:31.210 --> 03:32.587
I'm just worried.

03:32.670 --> 03:34.881
And why would you worry about me?

03:35.632 --> 03:37.133
Do you really not know?

03:38.301 --> 03:39.761
From morning until night,

03:40.303 --> 03:41.930
since childhood until now…

03:42.847 --> 03:46.059
It's been my fate and my task.
They're shackles weighing me down.

03:46.851 --> 03:49.979
I wonder if you're going around
acting like a decent human.

03:51.189 --> 03:53.983
I worry your mom will give you
a beating for saying something dumb.

03:54.067 --> 03:55.109
Hey!

03:55.193 --> 03:58.655
You've cried a bunch of times
after meeting so many bums.

03:59.572 --> 04:01.991
What else?
You get hit and shoved all the time.

04:03.076 --> 04:04.577
Are you a bumper car or something?

04:04.661 --> 04:07.956
This is a kitchen. It's full of sharp
and blunt objects, okay?

04:08.039 --> 04:10.166
That's why I'm worried you might get hurt.

04:11.668 --> 04:13.836
I wonder if you're skipping meals or not.

04:16.256 --> 04:17.131
And I hope…

04:18.341 --> 04:19.968
you have good people around you.

04:24.389 --> 04:25.723
That's just how I feel.

04:27.684 --> 04:28.685
So…

04:29.269 --> 04:30.812
think about…

04:32.188 --> 04:33.064
how you feel too.

04:36.276 --> 04:38.403
I know you just got out of a relationship.

04:39.153 --> 04:41.406
I know you're confused
because he's here too.

04:42.323 --> 04:44.409
So I'll give you some time.

04:47.578 --> 04:49.205
I answered you first…

04:53.084 --> 04:54.544
but you can answer me later.

04:59.549 --> 05:02.010
Gosh, it spilled everywhere.

05:02.093 --> 05:03.511
What were you boiling?

05:04.012 --> 05:05.722
I was going to make meatball soup.

06:05.323 --> 06:08.785
I left your gift in the nightstand drawer.
I hope you like it.

07:03.548 --> 07:04.757
This is prettier.

07:32.201 --> 07:33.077
Professor?

07:34.036 --> 07:36.122
You said it was
an important day, so you left early.

07:36.205 --> 07:37.331
Why are you back?

07:38.374 --> 07:39.750
I must have made a mistake.

07:41.169 --> 07:42.837
I thought it was over…

07:44.547 --> 07:45.882
but I guess not.

07:48.759 --> 07:50.553
Are you talking about work?

07:53.806 --> 07:55.892
Code blue.

07:55.975 --> 07:58.478
-Emergency medicine, TA code blue.
-Let's go.

08:03.107 --> 08:07.111
HIS SECRET

08:28.424 --> 08:30.259
You're really not going to swim?

08:31.677 --> 08:32.678
You don't like the water?

08:33.679 --> 08:34.805
Why?

08:34.889 --> 08:35.932
I'm scared.

08:36.516 --> 08:38.017
And I can't breathe.

08:38.893 --> 08:42.688
It's dark, and it feels like
something's pulling me down.

08:48.152 --> 08:49.570
In the water,

08:49.654 --> 08:52.782
you hear the same sounds
as when you cover your ears like this.

08:52.865 --> 08:54.867
So there's no need to be scared.

08:58.746 --> 09:00.289
Seung-hyo might not know,

09:01.040 --> 09:02.667
but I think I liked him first.

09:07.380 --> 09:11.092
It was when I was really young,
and I gradually forgot about it.

09:13.177 --> 09:15.596
Strangely, those feelings

09:16.305 --> 09:17.557
are still so vivid.

09:28.192 --> 09:29.860
But, Seung-hyo…

09:32.530 --> 09:33.656
is just Seung-hyo.

09:36.867 --> 09:38.369
You lunatic.

09:38.452 --> 09:40.121
I actually did it.

09:40.204 --> 09:42.248
Was I too hasty?

09:42.331 --> 09:43.958
Did I make it too overwhelming?

09:44.041 --> 09:45.960
No.

09:46.043 --> 09:49.630
If you've drawn the knife,
you should cut something.

09:49.714 --> 09:52.341
No, I think I cut something
I shouldn't have cut.

09:52.425 --> 09:53.384
No.

09:54.260 --> 09:55.344
It was decisive.

09:55.428 --> 09:57.930
It was good. I did great.

09:58.014 --> 09:59.974
I can't keep hesitating forever.

10:00.057 --> 10:01.851
But was that all I could say?

10:02.852 --> 10:04.770
That she was driving me crazy?

10:05.855 --> 10:07.148
This really is driving me crazy.

10:07.231 --> 10:09.317
That I was losing my mind because of her?

10:09.400 --> 10:11.527
I really am losing my mind. This is nuts.

10:13.487 --> 10:15.281
How do I face her tomorrow?

10:15.364 --> 10:16.657
Damn it.

10:19.201 --> 10:21.162
Damn it, I'm going to lose it.

10:49.273 --> 10:51.734
No, it wasn't too much for her.

10:51.817 --> 10:52.902
It wasn't.

10:52.985 --> 10:55.780
It was too much. Way too overwhelming.

10:56.447 --> 10:58.282
Damn it, how do I face her tomorrow?

10:58.366 --> 11:00.743
I won't… How could I not?

11:00.826 --> 11:02.953
Damn it, I'm going insane.

11:03.037 --> 11:04.455
Is she asleep right now?

11:08.918 --> 11:11.045
She's not asleep.

11:28.938 --> 11:30.398
This is insane.

11:31.941 --> 11:33.109
But why isn't she asleep?

11:35.152 --> 11:37.613
For crying out loud. Why isn't she asleep?

11:45.579 --> 11:47.665
This is driving me nuts.

11:47.748 --> 11:49.625
I think I was too hasty.

11:49.708 --> 11:51.127
I think I was.

12:05.015 --> 12:06.350
Why isn't she sleeping?

12:08.436 --> 12:10.187
Jeez, I'm going nuts.

12:22.700 --> 12:24.452
This is nuts.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.006
I didn't get any sleep.

12:43.429 --> 12:44.638
Good morning.

12:44.722 --> 12:46.265
Did you sleep well?

12:46.348 --> 12:47.933
Of course, I did.

12:49.477 --> 12:51.979
But you look a little tired.

12:52.646 --> 12:54.148
Did you have trouble sleeping?

12:55.816 --> 12:57.193
I was pretty busy.

12:57.693 --> 13:01.113
-Do you want coffee?
-No, I'll drink some tea today.

13:22.426 --> 13:23.636
Do you like your gift?

13:26.555 --> 13:28.641
I was waiting for you to notice.

13:29.517 --> 13:31.810
Yeah, I love it.

13:33.020 --> 13:36.482
You know so well exactly what I like.

13:37.650 --> 13:38.526
It looks good on you.

13:39.193 --> 13:43.280
Thanks. I'll cherish it forever.

13:43.948 --> 13:47.076
I'll get you something nicer next time.

13:50.246 --> 13:53.040
Come on. You promised. It's for real.

13:53.123 --> 13:53.958
Of course.

13:54.041 --> 13:57.253
Wow, I can't wait.

14:02.007 --> 14:02.841
Welcome home.

14:04.051 --> 14:06.929
Were you on night duty?
It was Mom's birthday yesterday.

14:09.098 --> 14:10.057
Was it?

14:11.517 --> 14:13.394
I was so busy. I must have forgotten.

14:14.186 --> 14:16.021
-I'm sorry.
-It's fine.

14:16.105 --> 14:18.440
Birthdays come every year.
They're not important.

14:19.275 --> 14:22.736
-It's late, but let's have a meal--
-I should go in and rest.

14:23.821 --> 14:25.698
I'm a bit tired.

14:44.049 --> 14:46.802
Jeez, look at these bags under my eyes.

14:46.886 --> 14:49.054
The Grim Reaper would look better than me.

15:01.358 --> 15:04.069
Hey, stop the blood with this.

15:04.153 --> 15:05.863
You'll get blood on it.
Isn't it expensive?

15:05.946 --> 15:07.698
That's not important.

15:07.781 --> 15:09.617
Why would you come here? It's dangerous.

15:10.242 --> 15:13.162
Who wipes a nosebleed
with something like that?

15:14.455 --> 15:15.789
I should give this back.

15:25.090 --> 15:27.301
Gosh, the windows weren't even open.

15:27.384 --> 15:30.220
Where does all this dust come from?

15:35.476 --> 15:37.394
-Mom.
-What?

15:37.978 --> 15:39.188
I was wondering

15:39.271 --> 15:41.941
if you've ever thought about investing?

15:43.317 --> 15:44.151
Investing?

15:44.234 --> 15:45.069
Yeah.

15:46.111 --> 15:49.239
I'm sure you've heard,
but it's the era of marketing these days.

15:49.323 --> 15:52.451
It's become crucial for fitness trainers
to promote themselves.

15:53.869 --> 15:55.371
Have you heard of Instargram?

15:55.454 --> 15:58.540
Yeah. You take pictures
with your phone and post them, right?

15:58.624 --> 15:59.583
I saw it on TV.

15:59.667 --> 16:01.460
I knew it. You're so trendy.

16:02.795 --> 16:05.798
You can become an influencer
if you get famous on Instargram.

16:05.881 --> 16:09.510
Then, you'll be able to rake in
all the money in this country--

16:09.593 --> 16:12.554
How dare you go
and spew your nonsense again?

16:13.764 --> 16:15.224
Hey.

16:15.307 --> 16:19.520
Excuse me, my dear older sister.
How about you butt out?

16:19.603 --> 16:22.106
I'm only 13 months older than you.

16:22.189 --> 16:25.484
Where the hell do you get off
acting as if you're some cool kid?

16:25.567 --> 16:27.236
Did you forget what your face value is?

16:28.028 --> 16:29.029
You know,

16:29.822 --> 16:33.409
I was going to live the rest of my life
in a beautiful, nonviolent way…

16:33.492 --> 16:34.326
Jeez!

16:34.410 --> 16:36.912
Are you two fighting
in front of your mother this morning?

16:37.913 --> 16:40.791
Mom, let's continue
our deep conversation later.

16:40.874 --> 16:42.126
Mom, don't listen to this punk.

16:43.002 --> 16:44.420
You say that nonsense again,

16:44.503 --> 16:46.797
and I'll end your life. Got it?

16:46.880 --> 16:48.090
-Yeah, right.
-Enough.

16:51.176 --> 16:53.387
Why aren't you in a T-shirt today?

16:54.179 --> 16:55.222
I put them in the laundry.

16:55.305 --> 16:57.766
No way. I folded several of them
and put them in your room.

16:57.850 --> 16:58.767
No, they're gone.

17:01.603 --> 17:02.688
You wore perfume too?

17:03.564 --> 17:04.565
Me?

17:05.107 --> 17:07.151
Yeah, you.

17:08.569 --> 17:11.488
Very fragrant.

17:26.503 --> 17:28.505
Did… Did you sleep well?

17:28.589 --> 17:29.423
Of course!

17:30.007 --> 17:34.011
I was stretched out comfortably
and slept without any thought. You?

17:34.094 --> 17:37.556
When I lay down and closed my eyes
for a second, it was morning.

17:37.639 --> 17:39.808
I snored so much my nose is sore.

17:39.892 --> 17:42.352
I was grinding my teeth so much
I thought I dislocated my jaw.

17:43.937 --> 17:46.607
-You grind your teeth in your sleep?
-What?

17:48.025 --> 17:49.109
I almost forgot.

17:51.153 --> 17:54.156
Thanks for letting me use this.
I appreciate it.

17:54.239 --> 17:55.449
Look. I got all the blood out.

17:57.576 --> 17:59.161
I wish it hadn't come out.

17:59.244 --> 18:01.288
Why? To ask for something better?

18:01.371 --> 18:03.373
No, so I could be buried in it later.

18:03.457 --> 18:05.167
It would've looked pretty nice.

18:05.667 --> 18:08.670
Are you insane? Do you think
you're in some melodrama or something?

18:09.296 --> 18:11.799
And why would you be buried?
We have to make it to 100.

18:12.633 --> 18:14.301
Make it to 100? Together?

18:15.511 --> 18:17.137
No, I misspoke.

18:17.930 --> 18:20.641
You know that saying
about living for a long time…

18:20.724 --> 18:22.059
-What?
-Good health and longevity.

18:22.142 --> 18:24.436
Eternal life and 100 years of marital…

18:24.520 --> 18:27.648
I mean, there's a saying
that's about 100 years.

18:28.148 --> 18:30.025
What was it? A hundred years…

18:30.109 --> 18:31.318
What's wrong with me?

18:32.528 --> 18:35.030
So about my answer…

18:36.406 --> 18:37.950
Can I really tell you later?

18:38.033 --> 18:41.703
Yeah, think about it
thoroughly and carefully.

18:41.787 --> 18:42.621
Really?

18:45.374 --> 18:47.835
Does that mean your answer
has no expiration date?

18:48.544 --> 18:49.962
Still,

18:50.045 --> 18:52.965
life is finite,
so no expiration date is a bit unfair.

18:53.048 --> 18:54.299
I guess so.

18:55.843 --> 18:56.885
Then…

19:01.473 --> 19:04.852
We should decide on an item.
How about canned goods?

19:06.228 --> 19:07.646
Aren't there too many kinds?

19:08.689 --> 19:11.316
Peaches, pineapples,

19:11.400 --> 19:13.610
corn, ham.

19:13.694 --> 19:15.904
-Tuna.
-Let's go with whelks.

19:18.365 --> 19:19.741
The expiration date is…

19:21.368 --> 19:23.412
Three years? Hey, that's too long.

19:23.495 --> 19:24.955
Then, what about Pacific saury?

19:28.792 --> 19:30.085
No stainless steel cans.

19:36.592 --> 19:37.759
How about instant rice?

19:39.636 --> 19:41.138
This has six months left.

19:42.556 --> 19:44.016
This one is eight months.

19:44.766 --> 19:47.019
-This one's for a year.
-How about this stuff?

19:50.731 --> 19:54.693
Your period of careful deliberation
lasts as long as refrigerated foods?

19:56.320 --> 19:59.948
You said I could answer later.
You told me to think it through carefully.

20:00.532 --> 20:03.118
The depth of thought is more important
than how long it takes.

20:06.622 --> 20:08.207
Since they're fermented,

20:08.290 --> 20:11.210
don't yogurt drinks have
the longest shelf life?

20:12.044 --> 20:13.295
Let's go with milk.

20:13.378 --> 20:15.380
Why did you even bother to ask then?

20:16.924 --> 20:18.508
But it'll be based on the back row.

20:19.927 --> 20:20.886
Deal.

20:36.151 --> 20:39.154
Hey, there's plain milk
and strawberry milk.

20:39.238 --> 20:42.783
There's also chocolate, banana,
and coffee. Which one do we pick?

20:45.410 --> 20:48.664
Did she leave? When did she go?

20:50.832 --> 20:54.461
Then, I'm going to pick the one
with the shortest shelf life.

20:58.257 --> 20:59.341
Excuse me.

21:00.509 --> 21:01.885
I've been watching you.

21:03.136 --> 21:04.721
-What are you doing?
-What?

21:04.805 --> 21:09.518
I barely make minimum wage,
and I had neatly arranged all of those.

21:09.601 --> 21:12.437
What am I supposed to do
if you mess them up like that?

21:15.983 --> 21:17.067
I'm sorry.

21:19.987 --> 21:21.029
You scared me.

21:21.113 --> 21:22.572
What's this?

21:22.656 --> 21:24.491
Snacks. Share them with everyone.

21:25.867 --> 21:27.911
You're so heartless.

21:27.995 --> 21:30.247
Hey, don't you know
I'm lactose intolerant?

21:30.330 --> 21:31.665
There are canned goods too.

21:32.916 --> 21:33.875
Hey, wait.

21:34.459 --> 21:36.420
I get why you'd buy
pineapples and peaches,

21:36.503 --> 21:39.256
but why did you buy
Pacific saury and whelks?

21:39.339 --> 21:41.967
I'll take this one. I'm on a diet.

21:42.718 --> 21:44.803
Sorry, but this one's mine.

21:44.886 --> 21:46.430
-But you like banana milk.
-Really?

21:46.513 --> 21:47.514
Yeah.

21:47.597 --> 21:51.685
I normally do,
but this one has the shortest shelf life.

21:54.813 --> 21:57.357
Goodness. Why did he smile like that?

21:57.441 --> 21:58.734
I have butterflies.

21:59.484 --> 22:01.945
Whelks for breakfast? Gosh.

22:03.530 --> 22:04.823
How about a can of beer?

22:07.034 --> 22:07.951
Soju?

22:09.161 --> 22:10.037
Soju and beer?

22:11.330 --> 22:14.833
-You want to write about your experiences?
-Yes, one special per week.

22:16.251 --> 22:17.836
It's a trend these days.

22:17.919 --> 22:21.048
Pick a topic each week, cover it,
and write an article on it.

22:21.131 --> 22:24.968
Can you do it?
Didn't you want to transfer departments?

22:25.052 --> 22:28.055
In movies,
superheroes always have two jobs.

22:28.138 --> 22:29.598
They have two personas too.

22:30.098 --> 22:34.269
I'm just an ordinary person,
but I wanted to give it a try.

22:34.352 --> 22:36.688
Can I ask you why
you suddenly changed your mind?

22:37.355 --> 22:40.525
I received the undeserving title
of Mudflat Man.

22:41.651 --> 22:43.820
-What?
-You won't kill the idea, will you?

22:45.030 --> 22:46.823
What's with that confidence?

22:48.158 --> 22:48.992
Okay.

22:49.743 --> 22:51.620
Where will you go first?

22:51.703 --> 22:53.663
HYEREUNG 911 SAFETY CENTER

22:53.747 --> 22:54.664
Excuse me?

22:54.748 --> 22:57.000
An emergency responder for a day?

22:57.084 --> 22:59.127
Yes, I'm here for the experience,
not an interview.

22:59.211 --> 23:03.632
I'm here to participate, not observe.
I'll work your hours and respond to calls.

23:03.715 --> 23:06.426
-But…
-Don't worry.

23:06.927 --> 23:08.720
I won't cause any inconvenience.

23:08.804 --> 23:10.972
Yes, but you can't just will that
to happen.

23:11.723 --> 23:15.393
From what I can see, I don't think
you'll be able to ride the ambulance.

23:15.477 --> 23:18.980
And I don't think you'll be able
to carry anything heavy either.

23:21.233 --> 23:22.609
Goodness.

23:23.360 --> 23:24.361
What are you doing?

23:24.444 --> 23:26.655
I want to clear up
any misunderstandings about me.

23:26.738 --> 23:28.281
I'm confident in my stamina.

23:28.365 --> 23:30.408
Not just anyone can survive
the social affairs team.

23:33.745 --> 23:35.580
Please help me out!

23:35.664 --> 23:37.457
I want to be in the field,
not behind a desk,

23:37.541 --> 23:39.543
and put my body to use
to write a good article.

23:39.626 --> 23:42.170
All right. I get it.

23:42.254 --> 23:44.422
Goodness. Please get up.
What are you doing?

23:44.506 --> 23:47.300
I said it's not up to me. Please stop.

23:47.384 --> 23:48.927
Who do I need permission from?

23:49.970 --> 23:50.887
What?

23:51.471 --> 23:54.724
Mr. Kang, I look forward to your article.

23:54.808 --> 23:57.686
Thank you, sir. I look forward
to working with you.

23:58.687 --> 24:01.314
Also, feel free to let me know
if you need anything.

24:01.398 --> 24:03.900
-Yes, sir.
-There she is. That's Jung Mo-eum.

24:03.984 --> 24:06.153
She'll be responsible for helping you.

24:08.321 --> 24:09.447
I'll be on my way now.

24:10.323 --> 24:14.119
Wow, I didn't think he'd be good
with people enough to be a reporter.

24:14.202 --> 24:16.454
But he's totally sociable.

24:17.247 --> 24:19.082
-What was that?
-Yeah.

24:19.166 --> 24:20.000
What?

24:26.715 --> 24:27.924
Why is this here?

24:30.886 --> 24:32.262
Did I leave this here?

24:40.312 --> 24:41.271
What on earth?

24:43.481 --> 24:45.859
I wiped everything down before I left.

24:45.942 --> 24:46.943
Why is this dirty?

24:48.612 --> 24:49.487
What?

24:51.281 --> 24:52.282
Gosh.

24:53.283 --> 24:54.451
Did I not wipe it down?

24:57.662 --> 24:58.622
What?

24:59.915 --> 25:00.749
What is this?

25:00.832 --> 25:02.167
Your delivery's here, sir!

25:02.250 --> 25:03.710
Hey.

25:03.793 --> 25:05.795
You're already working hard this early.

25:05.879 --> 25:07.380
Well, that's how work is.

25:07.464 --> 25:09.674
Today, it's two radishes,
two cabbages, two carrots,

25:09.758 --> 25:11.176
and a bag of onions, right?

25:11.259 --> 25:12.135
Okay.

25:14.471 --> 25:15.305
Excuse me?

25:16.932 --> 25:18.141
Have we met somewhere…

25:18.225 --> 25:20.810
Watching this show has been
my source of pleasure these days.

25:20.894 --> 25:22.187
-It's so good.
-Yeah.

25:22.270 --> 25:25.732
What was that actress's name?
She's become the nation's sweetheart.

25:25.815 --> 25:27.442
Hey, do you watch this show too?

25:27.525 --> 25:29.653
No, it's such a waste of time to watch TV.

25:29.736 --> 25:30.862
I'd rather read.

25:30.946 --> 25:32.822
Of course, you would.

25:32.906 --> 25:34.115
So what's it about?

25:34.199 --> 25:38.078
It's a romance story. It's about a man
and woman falling in love.

25:38.161 --> 25:40.121
See? It's so predictable.

25:40.205 --> 25:43.458
Most things are predictable.
And it's what everyone likes.

25:43.541 --> 25:45.752
-Yeah, right.
-Jeez.

25:47.212 --> 25:48.838
Yeah, I like that actor too.

25:48.922 --> 25:51.007
-Yeah, me too.
-Me too.

25:51.675 --> 25:53.218
So how did the two meet?

25:53.301 --> 25:54.636
They met abroad.

25:54.719 --> 25:56.096
HYEON-JUN: COULD WE MEET?

25:56.179 --> 25:57.639
It was so romantic too.

26:22.956 --> 26:23.873
My battery's dead.

26:27.752 --> 26:29.087
I didn't bring my charger.

26:35.010 --> 26:36.219
-Use mine.
-What?

26:38.013 --> 26:40.724
It seems urgent. You can use my charger.

26:42.392 --> 26:44.644
Okay. Thank you so much.

26:48.815 --> 26:51.234
But it might be too loud
if I take the call here.

26:52.319 --> 26:53.403
It's fine.

26:56.740 --> 26:57.615
Thank you.

27:28.521 --> 27:30.398
Thank you for meeting with me.

27:30.482 --> 27:31.900
I didn't come for you.

27:32.484 --> 27:35.278
I wanted to hear what you had to say.

27:35.362 --> 27:39.407
Let's order your coffee first.
We can order some cake too.

27:39.491 --> 27:42.452
You used to love cheesecake.

27:42.535 --> 27:43.787
Why did you do it?

27:43.870 --> 27:46.122
Seeing you two together
made me happy and content.

27:47.290 --> 27:48.333
Why did you do it?

27:48.416 --> 27:49.751
I'm sorry.

27:50.627 --> 27:53.880
I don't have any excuses I can give.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.548
You didn't cheat on each other.

27:55.632 --> 27:57.342
But you both won't tell me why.

27:58.802 --> 28:00.553
You're all so tight-lipped.

28:02.931 --> 28:04.015
You've already broken up,

28:04.099 --> 28:06.684
so I can't weld
or patch things together again.

28:07.602 --> 28:11.022
But I can't let it go,
because it's all so strange.

28:13.024 --> 28:15.860
If you called off the wedding,
you must've seen each other's worst.

28:15.944 --> 28:20.698
-How come you don't hate each other?
-I've never hated her.

28:21.324 --> 28:24.911
I still love Seok-ryu.

28:35.839 --> 28:36.881
What's this?

28:38.591 --> 28:39.592
What?

28:41.344 --> 28:43.054
Why the hell is she with him?

28:53.857 --> 28:55.734
I took this from the back row.

28:55.817 --> 28:57.736
EXPIRATION DATE JUNE 29

28:57.819 --> 28:59.904
Only 11 days?

29:01.322 --> 29:04.951
My goodness. Excuse me. I'm so sorry.

29:05.577 --> 29:09.122
That's okay.
Seok-ryu's roar woke everyone up.

29:10.123 --> 29:12.333
Okay, shall we start class?

29:12.417 --> 29:13.752
-Yes, ma'am.
-All right.

29:18.089 --> 29:20.175
I'll have to store this well.

29:25.054 --> 29:28.975
Stay fresh in here.
I'll see you in 11 days.

29:36.024 --> 29:37.233
You scared me.

29:38.234 --> 29:40.069
Why are you sitting there like that?

29:41.946 --> 29:43.656
Did you close up and come home?

29:43.740 --> 29:45.450
No customers again?

29:46.034 --> 29:47.410
Why did you meet Hyeon-jun?

29:49.329 --> 29:50.163
What?

29:52.707 --> 29:55.001
Did you think I wouldn't know
if you kept it from me?

29:57.045 --> 29:59.214
I'm Seok-ryu's dad.

30:00.089 --> 30:02.675
How much more of a fool
will you make of me?

30:02.759 --> 30:04.636
Don't say it like that.

30:05.929 --> 30:08.097
I met him,
because he suddenly contacted me.

30:08.181 --> 30:09.599
I was going to tell you.

30:12.560 --> 30:13.728
What did that punk say?

30:13.812 --> 30:16.564
He said he still loves Seok-ryu.

30:17.148 --> 30:18.817
He wants to go back to the US with her.

30:18.900 --> 30:21.236
How dare that bastard say that?

30:22.862 --> 30:23.905
So what about you?

30:24.739 --> 30:27.659
You just sat there
and listened to him as he said that?

30:28.284 --> 30:31.037
I told you.
I'm all for Seok-ryu going back.

30:31.120 --> 30:33.206
Jeez, there you go again
with that US nonsense!

30:34.332 --> 30:36.459
Are you obsessed with the US or something?

30:37.085 --> 30:39.337
-Are you trying to sell your daughter off?
-What?

30:39.420 --> 30:41.005
You know how you are.

30:41.089 --> 30:44.634
As long as the conditions are met
and it makes people jealous,

30:44.717 --> 30:47.011
you don't care,
no matter how Seok-ryu feels!

30:47.095 --> 30:49.389
That's right. I am self-serving.

30:50.265 --> 30:52.934
She'd send me bags
from US outlet stores every season.

30:53.017 --> 30:56.271
She even sent shoes,
but I'm heartbroken now that's all gone.

30:56.354 --> 30:58.940
So what? I was hoping to brag
that my son-in-law was a lawyer.

30:59.023 --> 31:01.067
But I'm sad it's over now.
Are you happy?

31:05.071 --> 31:07.657
Look, I just…

31:08.950 --> 31:11.703
I don't want her
to be a failure and live like me.

31:12.537 --> 31:15.665
I don't want her
to live a poor, shabby life!

31:31.890 --> 31:33.349
You don't know anything.

31:34.392 --> 31:35.768
Damn it.

31:56.080 --> 31:57.498
-Hey, Gyeong-jong…
-Geun-sik…

31:59.125 --> 32:00.752
Do you want to get a drink?

32:00.835 --> 32:02.670
That's what I wanted to ask.

32:02.754 --> 32:04.255
-Okay, let's go.
-Okay.

32:07.842 --> 32:08.927
Gyeong-jong.

32:11.054 --> 32:13.973
What's it like to live as someone

32:14.766 --> 32:17.018
who's successful like you?

32:17.101 --> 32:19.187
Is it nice like this crunchy fried squid?

32:21.940 --> 32:23.024
For me,

32:23.900 --> 32:28.196
my life's like this soggy piece. So soggy.

32:28.279 --> 32:30.657
It's soaked in my feelings of inferiority.

32:34.118 --> 32:37.538
Since I'm incompetent,
I worried something went wrong.

32:37.622 --> 32:41.042
I was so scared
that I couldn't even ask why.

32:41.125 --> 32:44.671
All I could do was pester my wife.

32:46.839 --> 32:48.675
Mine's bone dry.

32:50.051 --> 32:52.387
My family could crumble
at the slightest touch.

32:55.598 --> 32:57.642
But this tteokbokki…

32:57.725 --> 32:58.559
Yeah?

32:59.686 --> 33:03.106
Is it made from flour or rice?

33:03.189 --> 33:04.399
This?

33:05.400 --> 33:07.735
This is made from rice.

33:09.821 --> 33:11.155
Why?

33:11.239 --> 33:14.033
Don't get me wrong.
Ones made with flour are good too, but…

33:15.243 --> 33:16.619
I like ones made with rice.

33:19.330 --> 33:21.624
-Why?
-Because it's…

33:22.208 --> 33:24.210
It's so chewy.

33:25.753 --> 33:30.216
But usually, snack shops
often sell ones made with flour.

33:31.009 --> 33:31.968
Why?

33:32.844 --> 33:37.181
Well, because it's…
So this is what you're curious about?

33:37.265 --> 33:41.185
Ones made with rice bloat more
and get soggy more easily.

33:41.269 --> 33:44.647
The sauce doesn't soak all the way in,
so it's tricky.

33:45.606 --> 33:46.774
Why?

33:47.442 --> 33:53.990
Well, because that's how they are.
And so, I told you why.

33:54.782 --> 33:56.659
But you keep asking me why,

33:56.743 --> 34:01.080
so I'm telling you why the ones
made with rice are naturally like that.

34:02.040 --> 34:02.999
Why?

34:03.082 --> 34:04.042
Damn it.

34:09.047 --> 34:11.883
I'm trying to be serious here.

34:12.717 --> 34:15.553
Why do you keep joking around?

34:18.222 --> 34:20.058
This tteokbokki…

34:22.351 --> 34:25.730
Is it made from flour or rice?

34:25.813 --> 34:28.357
Jeez, this guy has
a terrible habit when drunk.

34:29.609 --> 34:32.445
Why did you go back to the start?
What are you, a repeat sign?

34:32.528 --> 34:34.655
Come on.

34:34.739 --> 34:37.075
-Why?
-Stop it! I swear!

34:37.158 --> 34:38.951
It's scaring me now.

34:45.166 --> 34:46.209
Goodness.

34:47.085 --> 34:48.294
That scared me.

34:51.964 --> 34:52.924
What is this?

34:54.801 --> 34:56.052
Why is this here?

35:00.056 --> 35:01.224
Did you…

35:01.974 --> 35:03.267
put this here?

35:03.351 --> 35:06.145
-What is that?
-I don't know. I've never seen it before.

35:06.229 --> 35:07.772
I don't know either.

35:12.944 --> 35:15.321
Wait, did it break?

35:27.125 --> 35:29.001
Lily of the valley…

35:29.085 --> 35:32.171
Lily of the valley…

35:32.255 --> 35:38.136
Why do you keep saying
"lily of the valley" over and over again?

35:38.219 --> 35:40.638
Why? Lily of the valley… What?

35:40.721 --> 35:43.391
Are you talking about the song?

35:45.852 --> 35:50.064
Late night at Mapo Terminal

35:50.815 --> 35:53.985
A night train with nowhere to go

35:54.986 --> 35:56.237
Lily of the valley.

35:57.488 --> 35:58.698
Lily of the valley…

35:58.781 --> 36:01.826
What is it then? It's not the song?

36:02.535 --> 36:04.328
-Lily of the valley…
-Yeah?

36:05.204 --> 36:07.373
-They're her favorite.
-They are?

36:07.456 --> 36:08.291
No.

36:09.125 --> 36:10.960
-They were her favorite.
-Okay.

36:14.255 --> 36:16.299
They were hard to find.

36:16.382 --> 36:21.262
So you had a hard time
finding lily of the valleys, Gyeong-jong?

36:21.345 --> 36:23.097
Okay, then.

36:23.181 --> 36:24.515
I'll get them for you.

36:25.099 --> 36:26.350
I'll do it.

36:26.434 --> 36:28.769
I'll get them for you. Wait here.

36:28.853 --> 36:30.396
Wait right there.

36:31.564 --> 36:34.901
I'm going to get you
those lily of the valleys.

36:34.984 --> 36:37.403
I'm off to get them.

37:20.488 --> 37:22.698
That fool. What gives him the right?

37:22.782 --> 37:26.118
Now, he spends the entire night out?
Unbelievable.

37:28.329 --> 37:30.539
You've never done this before.
You're scaring me.

37:30.623 --> 37:32.708
A son can't help his mom do the dishes?

37:34.001 --> 37:36.087
Use hot water. Get rid of the grease.

37:38.923 --> 37:40.174
Wash that too.

37:40.258 --> 37:42.134
As I do the dishes,

37:42.218 --> 37:46.430
shall we continue
our conversation from before?

37:46.514 --> 37:47.598
-Give them back!
-Come now!

37:48.307 --> 37:50.309
Don't be like that. Hear me out, Mom.

37:51.394 --> 37:53.604
In order to become an influencer,

37:53.688 --> 37:55.690
I need admirers… No, worshippers.

37:55.773 --> 37:57.066
I need followers.

37:58.150 --> 38:00.820
Why would people follow you?
Based on what?

38:00.903 --> 38:02.947
You're so objective. Right?

38:03.030 --> 38:04.031
Yeah.

38:04.115 --> 38:08.536
So that's why
you can buy followers with money.

38:08.619 --> 38:11.455
With tens of thousands,
they say you can live comfortably.

38:11.539 --> 38:14.208
You can do group buying
and get sponsorships.

38:14.292 --> 38:17.044
I only have two million won.

38:17.128 --> 38:19.046
Mom, it's an investment.

38:19.130 --> 38:21.424
That's not nearly enough.

38:22.174 --> 38:23.634
-You damn lunatic.
-Damn it.

38:23.718 --> 38:25.636
-Come here.
-Hey!

38:25.720 --> 38:28.848
You punk. A parasite would have
more of a conscience than you.

38:28.931 --> 38:31.392
You've mooched off
your parents your whole life.

38:31.475 --> 38:33.811
And you still want to live like that
in your thirties?

38:33.894 --> 38:35.104
Damn it.

38:35.646 --> 38:37.690
Hey, watch your mouth.

38:37.773 --> 38:39.442
You better watch how you act.

38:39.525 --> 38:43.404
You always have your head in the clouds
instead of working hard to earn money.

38:44.822 --> 38:46.449
Don't you even feel bad for Mom?

38:46.532 --> 38:49.410
Cut the crap.
What makes you different from me?

38:50.244 --> 38:51.162
What?

38:52.455 --> 38:53.956
Say that again.

38:54.040 --> 38:55.499
-Hey, that's enough!
-What?

38:55.583 --> 38:57.501
I already have
a terrible headache as it is.

38:57.585 --> 39:00.504
Why do you two always fight
whenever you see each other?

39:00.588 --> 39:02.465
Seok-ryu, stop it. Dong-jin, go inside.

39:04.550 --> 39:07.011
-You're the worst.
-You have no right to act mad.

39:10.514 --> 39:11.515
Mom.

39:12.099 --> 39:13.851
That punk's tricked you before.

39:13.934 --> 39:16.103
You better not give him any money.

39:16.187 --> 39:18.564
-I'll take care of it.
-What do you mean?

39:18.647 --> 39:21.567
He's like that
because you always baby him!

39:21.650 --> 39:22.985
That's because…

39:24.153 --> 39:28.115
he's had a hole in his heart since birth.

39:28.199 --> 39:31.285
So the doctor said not to make him cry
since he might need surgery.

39:31.369 --> 39:32.870
I've heard it a thousand times.

39:33.579 --> 39:35.206
But he didn't have surgery.

39:35.289 --> 39:38.542
The hole closed up on its own.
You should've been stricter on him.

39:38.626 --> 39:41.545
How could you let him be this immature
for so long?

39:41.629 --> 39:43.214
Try having kids of your own.

39:43.297 --> 39:45.549
See if you can treat
your sick child that way.

39:47.051 --> 39:48.552
Are you taking his side again?

39:50.012 --> 39:51.764
Is being sick that big of a deal?

40:11.450 --> 40:13.327
THERE ARE TEN DAYS LEFT

40:13.411 --> 40:18.457
HAVE A GOOD DAY TODAY

40:21.961 --> 40:23.170
Damn.

40:26.215 --> 40:29.176
-What are you doing?
-What? Nothing. Let's go in.

40:29.260 --> 40:30.469
-Take this.
-Okay.

40:34.640 --> 40:36.016
There are ten days left.

40:36.100 --> 40:37.435
Have a good day today.

40:37.518 --> 40:39.895
Did he just send me an emoji?

40:41.188 --> 40:43.649
He's never done this before.

40:44.608 --> 40:45.943
Did something good happen?

40:47.736 --> 40:48.904
Hyeon-jun.

40:49.697 --> 40:52.158
I'm glad I caught you before it got cold.

40:52.867 --> 40:54.243
What is this?

40:54.326 --> 40:55.244
It's jasmine tea.

40:56.871 --> 40:58.122
I've changed my strategy.

40:58.622 --> 41:01.625
The "lasts" didn't work,
so I'm going back to the beginning.

41:13.095 --> 41:16.182
You looked busy earlier,
so I didn't get a chance to tell you.

41:16.265 --> 41:17.766
Thank you for the charger.

41:17.850 --> 41:19.185
I owe you one.

41:19.268 --> 41:20.603
It was no big deal.

41:20.686 --> 41:22.104
Yes, it was.

41:22.188 --> 41:24.982
On that note, can I treat you to a drink?

41:25.649 --> 41:26.817
No, it's okay.

41:26.901 --> 41:28.152
It's not okay with me.

41:28.903 --> 41:30.237
I'll buy you some coffee.

41:32.406 --> 41:33.616
But the coffee here…

41:34.200 --> 41:35.284
isn't good.

41:35.367 --> 41:36.410
I see.

41:41.707 --> 41:43.042
Do you like osam-bulgogi?

41:43.125 --> 41:44.543
What?

41:45.127 --> 41:46.670
-You don't?
-I do.

41:48.088 --> 41:49.089
Let's go then.

42:07.942 --> 42:09.401
It's jasmine tea.

42:09.485 --> 42:12.488
-Why are you giving me this?
-It's good for digestive health.

42:12.988 --> 42:15.741
It looked like you were drinking
too much coffee.

42:16.992 --> 42:18.077
I'll be outside.

42:38.264 --> 42:39.807
I'm going to start over again.

42:41.058 --> 42:42.226
If I do that,

42:42.309 --> 42:45.187
you might smile at me as you did before.

42:48.941 --> 42:50.359
Well, that's it for today.

42:51.318 --> 42:52.361
Bye.

43:03.205 --> 43:05.332
Maybe we shouldn't have done so well.

43:05.416 --> 43:07.418
I can't believe Fresco likes it already.

43:07.918 --> 43:08.836
Isn't that good?

43:09.587 --> 43:10.546
No.

43:11.088 --> 43:13.591
Then, our collaboration
will end too quickly.

43:13.674 --> 43:16.176
You should've drawn them
with your foot so they'd reject us.

43:16.260 --> 43:19.221
I wanted to be pressed by deadlines
so we could pull all-nighters.

43:19.305 --> 43:21.348
I'm way too competent for that.

43:23.017 --> 43:24.602
You know how to joke now?

43:24.685 --> 43:28.564
I'm mad for some reason. I think
you've become comfortable around me.

43:29.273 --> 43:31.358
I walked into the fire on my own.

43:31.859 --> 43:35.487
Like you said, you won't know
what happens until it goes in the kiln.

43:36.905 --> 43:38.699
Wait, did you…

43:41.410 --> 43:43.287
I told Seok-ryu how I felt about her.

43:53.464 --> 43:54.757
What did she say?

43:56.425 --> 43:57.968
She hasn't answered me yet.

43:59.553 --> 44:02.056
I see you're stuck in that kiln
with nowhere to go.

44:03.849 --> 44:05.142
You could say that.

44:05.225 --> 44:07.603
I hope it cracks.

44:07.686 --> 44:10.522
I hope it swells up inside and bursts.

44:10.606 --> 44:14.526
I'm already burning and suffering.
I don't need your help as it is.

44:17.112 --> 44:18.739
So this is how it turns out.

44:19.990 --> 44:23.202
Is this why people say men
and women can't be friends?

44:24.411 --> 44:27.331
The reason why I can't stay
as Seok-ryu's friend

44:27.414 --> 44:28.916
isn't because she's a woman.

44:32.920 --> 44:34.338
It's because she's Seok-ryu.

44:37.341 --> 44:38.926
It makes me angry, but I agree.

44:39.635 --> 44:42.971
I don't think you deceived me
while having feelings for her either.

44:44.056 --> 44:47.810
You were a great person
when we dated.

44:50.979 --> 44:54.191
I was very emotional back then.

44:55.984 --> 44:58.570
I'd be crouched in a dark corner alone,

44:58.654 --> 45:01.156
and you'd always bring me
back into the light.

45:03.117 --> 45:04.410
That's probably why…

45:06.120 --> 45:07.621
I couldn't forget you.

45:11.792 --> 45:13.752
Does this mean I've been dumped?

45:15.170 --> 45:18.507
No, you could be dumped too.

45:19.299 --> 45:22.010
-What?
-The man from the restaurant that day.

45:22.761 --> 45:24.012
He seemed formidable.

45:24.721 --> 45:27.224
They seemed pretty close.

45:28.183 --> 45:29.226
Not to mention,

45:29.309 --> 45:32.813
he's a sexy and mature man who's at ease.

45:32.896 --> 45:34.940
Just out of curiosity,

45:35.023 --> 45:37.484
has the social perception
of what's sexy changed?

45:37.568 --> 45:40.237
Or should I be questioning
your eye for beauty?

45:41.363 --> 45:42.698
You're feeling threatened.

45:42.781 --> 45:43.824
Of course not.

45:44.575 --> 45:47.411
I'm only asking
as a concerned business partner.

45:49.955 --> 45:52.082
Call me if you come out
of the kiln broken.

45:52.166 --> 45:53.292
I'll buy you a drink.

45:54.293 --> 45:56.044
Why are you being so negative--

45:56.128 --> 45:57.337
Let's make it makgeolli.

45:58.046 --> 46:00.466
I'm not drinking. And I never will.

46:00.549 --> 46:03.218
Tell Myeong-u I'll send him
the bowl I promised soon.

46:18.525 --> 46:19.359
BAE DONG-JIN

46:19.443 --> 46:21.320
Seung-hyo, are you free tonight?

46:21.862 --> 46:23.071
TRANSFER 2,000,000 WON?

46:23.155 --> 46:25.616
Your transaction is being processed.
Do you need a receipt?

46:25.699 --> 46:27.910
TRANSACTION AMOUNT: 2,000,000 WON
BALANCE: 180,002 WON

46:27.993 --> 46:29.119
Please take your card.

46:29.203 --> 46:31.830
Please check if you have
all of your belongings.

46:31.914 --> 46:33.081
Thank you.

46:34.041 --> 46:35.667
Hey, it's been a while.

46:36.835 --> 46:38.253
No, it's just…

46:39.379 --> 46:41.840
I was wondering if you knew
of any good part-time jobs.

46:41.924 --> 46:43.300
That was so fun.

46:43.383 --> 46:45.052
-It's fun every day.
-What?

46:45.135 --> 46:46.428
No, like last time…

46:46.970 --> 46:48.514
I'll call you back later.

46:51.225 --> 46:54.311
Excuse me. What kind of place is this?

46:55.354 --> 46:56.605
It's a cooking school.

46:56.688 --> 46:58.941
We also hold cooking classes.

46:59.024 --> 47:00.275
-Cooking?
-Yes.

47:24.174 --> 47:25.050
Good grief.

47:30.097 --> 47:33.058
Mister, can I get an order of tteokbokki?

47:33.141 --> 47:35.269
Goodness, I'm sorry.

47:35.352 --> 47:37.646
I don't think I can sell this to you.

47:37.729 --> 47:39.856
Why not? You have so much.

47:40.816 --> 47:43.569
I don't think
I can sell this in good conscience.

47:43.652 --> 47:44.945
It's too soggy.

47:45.028 --> 47:46.196
What can you do?

47:46.280 --> 47:48.156
Okay. Goodbye.

47:48.240 --> 47:49.074
Goodness.

47:49.157 --> 47:51.118
I'm sorry. Come back next time.

47:56.039 --> 47:58.959
How about we start over again?

48:01.003 --> 48:03.213
That's right. It's the bag from before.

48:03.797 --> 48:05.924
What is this?

48:06.925 --> 48:09.595
What is this? I didn't put this in here.

48:10.178 --> 48:11.096
Honey.

48:11.847 --> 48:12.681
What?

48:15.183 --> 48:16.518
I'm home.

48:17.728 --> 48:18.604
Hi.

48:18.687 --> 48:21.106
Why are you sitting here?

48:22.274 --> 48:23.233
Is no one home?

48:23.859 --> 48:26.111
Dong-jin said he needed to talk to me.

48:26.653 --> 48:29.031
He said he'd be late
and told me to wait inside.

48:29.114 --> 48:30.866
Why would he need to talk to you?

48:31.533 --> 48:34.328
I don't know.
He said he has something to propose.

48:35.704 --> 48:37.956
Damn it. That bastard.

48:38.040 --> 48:39.833
He even asked you?

48:39.916 --> 48:42.502
This punk must be out of his mind.

48:43.587 --> 48:44.671
What? What is it?

48:45.631 --> 48:48.717
Mom, do you know what Dong-jin's doing?

48:48.800 --> 48:50.927
He asked you for money,
and now, he asked…

48:52.554 --> 48:54.139
KOREAN FOOD CRAFTSMAN
PRACTICAL SKILLS

48:56.308 --> 48:57.267
What are you doing?

48:57.351 --> 48:58.644
What is all of this?

48:58.727 --> 49:01.897
Mom, don't you think
this is a little much? Come on.

49:01.980 --> 49:04.024
Why are you inspecting stuff in my bag?

49:05.651 --> 49:06.693
What is all of this?

49:06.777 --> 49:08.695
Aunt Mi-suk, you should calm down first.

49:08.779 --> 49:09.946
-Sit down…
-Can't you tell?

49:10.447 --> 49:11.573
It's a cooking book.

49:13.116 --> 49:15.661
Why do you have it?
Why would you have this?

49:17.079 --> 49:18.872
Because I want to cook.

49:20.207 --> 49:21.083
What?

49:22.709 --> 49:25.337
Let's hear what she has to say first.

49:25.420 --> 49:26.797
She's had her reasons.

49:26.880 --> 49:30.300
Seung-hyo, did you know?
You knew she was taking cooking classes?

49:33.428 --> 49:34.262
Yeah.

49:34.346 --> 49:35.931
Goodness.

49:37.265 --> 49:39.351
After running wild
and being reckless together,

49:39.434 --> 49:40.894
were you conspiring together too?

49:40.977 --> 49:41.978
I'm sorry.

49:42.062 --> 49:44.189
-But--
-He didn't do anything wrong.

49:44.272 --> 49:47.150
-This is my business. My dream.
-How dare you?

49:47.234 --> 49:48.318
So…

49:49.152 --> 49:50.862
that's why you've been coming to my shop?

49:51.655 --> 49:53.532
To secretly use my kitchen?

49:54.825 --> 49:56.243
I'm sorry.

49:56.326 --> 49:58.036
I didn't have a place to practice.

49:59.371 --> 50:02.958
I was going to tell you both
after I got my certification.

50:03.041 --> 50:04.084
Certification?

50:04.584 --> 50:08.547
Seok-ryu, do you really want
to do this type of work?

50:09.965 --> 50:12.050
Yeah, I do.

50:13.510 --> 50:16.722
I worked really hard to find my dream.

50:16.805 --> 50:18.348
Goodness.

50:18.432 --> 50:20.308
What about your old work?

50:21.017 --> 50:22.102
Well?

50:22.185 --> 50:25.439
What about all the studying you did?
And your experience?

50:25.522 --> 50:28.567
It was a valuable experience.
That time is precious to me.

50:28.650 --> 50:29.609
But…

50:30.110 --> 50:33.739
I think this is where it ends, Dad.

50:49.254 --> 50:52.466
We raised a smart fool.

50:53.508 --> 50:58.555
Seok-ryu, did all of that praise
go to your head?

50:59.598 --> 51:01.975
-Dad…
-You couldn't stay at a job for ten years.

51:02.058 --> 51:04.644
Do you really think
you can handle this kind of work

51:05.687 --> 51:08.106
with that kind of mentality?

51:13.904 --> 51:14.780
What's going on?

51:15.947 --> 51:18.116
Why is the mood so awful again?

51:20.035 --> 51:21.578
Was it you again, Seok-ryu?

51:26.458 --> 51:29.461
Don't you two ever think
you're being too hard on me?

51:30.504 --> 51:32.464
Why are the standards different for me?

51:32.964 --> 51:35.008
Why are you so strict with me?

51:36.384 --> 51:38.178
What's Dong-jin done up until now?

51:38.720 --> 51:41.223
He wanted to be a soccer player,
but ran away from camp.

51:41.306 --> 51:43.600
He wanted to learn music,
so you bought him instruments,

51:43.683 --> 51:44.684
but he quit right after.

51:44.768 --> 51:47.270
He tried four times
and couldn't get into college.

51:47.854 --> 51:50.774
He joined a theater troupe
to be an actor, but quit immediately.

51:50.857 --> 51:52.484
Why the hell are you bringing the past?

51:52.567 --> 51:54.861
You know why
I've worked so hard up until now?

51:56.905 --> 51:59.825
You've both suffered so much
because of Dong-jin.

52:01.368 --> 52:04.287
I didn't want to add to your worries.

52:06.122 --> 52:08.166
But what is he doing now?

52:08.250 --> 52:11.127
He's got another wild idea,
and he's pestering you, Mom!

52:12.963 --> 52:13.797
Shut your mouth!

52:14.422 --> 52:15.841
Keep quiet.

52:15.924 --> 52:17.759
How do you always put up with him

52:19.386 --> 52:22.347
but never allow me to make
a single mistake?

52:23.056 --> 52:24.140
Why…

52:24.224 --> 52:26.726
Why can't I do what I want with my life?

52:27.686 --> 52:28.687
Fine.

52:31.273 --> 52:34.025
Seok-ryu, do whatever you want.
You can do it all.

52:34.985 --> 52:36.486
But not cooking.

52:38.113 --> 52:39.698
I'm sure it's fun now.

52:40.448 --> 52:45.203
You imagine your customers happily eating
your food in a charming restaurant.

52:45.287 --> 52:47.205
I'm sure it's like a fairy tale.

52:47.873 --> 52:49.082
I was like that too.

52:49.583 --> 52:50.917
That's why you can't.

52:52.043 --> 52:54.337
You can't because I've tried it. Okay?

52:57.257 --> 52:58.174
Hey.

52:59.384 --> 53:03.763
You're not the only one who feels wronged.
You're not the only victim!

53:03.847 --> 53:06.725
I've spent my entire life
being criticized by you!

53:06.808 --> 53:09.936
Damn it. So annoying.
As if she's the only one feeling wronged.

53:24.826 --> 53:26.161
Don't follow me.

53:28.997 --> 53:30.123
Follow me.

53:33.126 --> 53:34.836
How did you know about this place?

53:36.588 --> 53:38.715
I've kept it in mind for times like these.

53:39.257 --> 53:41.468
Times when I'd need to comfort someone.

53:43.136 --> 53:44.638
So you came here with Tae-hui.

53:47.182 --> 53:49.184
There's a thing called business ethics.

53:52.062 --> 53:53.355
But you know…

53:54.689 --> 53:58.151
knowing everything
about each other's past in detail

53:59.402 --> 54:01.571
isn't much of an advantage
for me right now.

54:03.156 --> 54:04.658
Look at those flowers!

54:05.158 --> 54:07.661
They're so white. They look like popcorn.

54:08.912 --> 54:12.749
How does your brain work?
How do you go from flowers to food?

54:12.832 --> 54:16.544
I mean, they look delicious.
I want to drizzle caramel over them.

54:17.212 --> 54:19.047
What do you think they're called?

54:19.798 --> 54:20.966
Bridalwreaths…

54:21.675 --> 54:25.470
are neighbors to these, the fringetree.

54:26.179 --> 54:27.931
They say the leaves look like rice.

54:28.014 --> 54:29.140
I see.

54:30.058 --> 54:33.436
Such interesting names.

54:40.485 --> 54:41.987
You're not tall enough.

54:43.154 --> 54:44.322
Damn.

54:46.199 --> 54:47.951
Do you feel a little better?

54:50.787 --> 54:52.414
I'm just a little embarrassed.

54:53.999 --> 54:57.377
How do you end up seeing
all of my embarrassing moments in life?

54:59.713 --> 55:02.215
I can recall all of your dark past…

55:02.298 --> 55:05.010
Wait, this won't help me much either.

55:07.262 --> 55:08.680
This is so annoying.

55:10.098 --> 55:12.225
I've felt so wronged for the longest time.

55:14.185 --> 55:16.521
I thought getting it off my chest

55:17.897 --> 55:19.941
would make me feel better.

55:20.942 --> 55:22.527
I only feel worse.

55:22.610 --> 55:23.987
I know that feeling.

55:25.780 --> 55:27.699
Parents aren't always right.

55:28.366 --> 55:30.493
They make mistakes
with their children too.

55:31.119 --> 55:34.414
When you argue over it,
you end up feeling guilty for no reason.

55:34.497 --> 55:35.832
Exactly.

55:37.250 --> 55:39.794
How did you know that?
Did you fight with your parents too?

55:40.795 --> 55:41.838
No.

55:42.422 --> 55:44.424
I'm so jealous of your family.

55:46.217 --> 55:50.847
Your parents are cultured,
and they watch what they say.

55:51.973 --> 55:55.935
Also, you don't have a dumbass sibling.

55:56.019 --> 55:58.605
I envy that the most.
When will that punk grow up?

56:02.275 --> 56:04.527
Where am I supposed
to practice cooking now?

56:06.279 --> 56:07.280
Do it at our office.

56:08.656 --> 56:11.409
-What?
-Use the kitchen after everyone leaves.

56:11.951 --> 56:14.079
Everyone's on a business trip this week.

56:15.038 --> 56:17.916
Still, I can't do that at your office.

56:18.625 --> 56:20.293
Did you forget I'm the president?

56:20.376 --> 56:23.296
You've gotten a taste for power.

56:23.379 --> 56:25.632
You can't be reckless
just because you're the boss.

56:25.715 --> 56:27.759
-You want to use it or not?
-I'll use it.

56:28.802 --> 56:30.011
But just once.

56:30.095 --> 56:32.138
And I didn't ask for this favor.

56:32.222 --> 56:33.640
You offered it to me first.

56:33.723 --> 56:34.974
Who's saying otherwise?

56:36.184 --> 56:37.227
Right.

56:39.145 --> 56:41.523
The view is nice.

56:43.024 --> 56:46.194
They really look like popcorn to me.

56:50.490 --> 56:51.783
It's past midnight.

56:52.659 --> 56:54.160
You have nine days left.

56:58.456 --> 56:59.582
Wait for me.

57:09.008 --> 57:10.093
HYEREUNG 911 SAFETY CENTER

57:10.176 --> 57:11.052
I'm Kang Dan-ho.

57:11.136 --> 57:13.054
It's nice to meet you.

57:15.223 --> 57:16.683
Welcome to the team!

57:17.350 --> 57:19.686
I heard you were coming,
and I couldn't sleep.

57:19.769 --> 57:20.937
Why?

57:21.020 --> 57:22.105
I was excited.

57:23.022 --> 57:24.607
Are we taking pictures today?

57:24.691 --> 57:26.276
I used a sheet mask last night.

57:26.359 --> 57:28.069
-Jeez.
-Are you here to have fun?

57:28.153 --> 57:29.571
Just act normal.

57:29.654 --> 57:31.531
That way, he'll know
how serious our job is.

57:32.323 --> 57:35.326
-Yes, sir.
-We all put our lives on the line.

57:35.410 --> 57:38.413
-You should know that.
-Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

57:44.461 --> 57:47.213
That last statement
sounded a bit old-fashioned even for me.

57:47.922 --> 57:50.216
He's a great person
when you get to know him.

57:50.300 --> 57:52.469
He has a very strong sense of duty too.

57:52.552 --> 57:54.429
I can tell even if you don't tell me.

57:55.138 --> 57:57.307
Okay. Shall we get going?

57:57.390 --> 57:58.391
Yes, ma'am!

58:08.860 --> 58:12.030
Okay. You're going to use
this locker for today.

58:12.113 --> 58:13.948
-Okay.
-Your basic equipment.

58:14.032 --> 58:17.368
You have your safety helmet,
vest, thermal jacket, and camera.

58:17.452 --> 58:21.372
You can put the camera on your vest
wherever it's comfortable for you.

58:21.456 --> 58:22.707
-Okay.
-Next.

58:22.790 --> 58:27.170
Now, we ride in this vehicle
when we're dispatched to a call.

58:27.253 --> 58:28.713
-Okay.
-Let me show you.

58:29.839 --> 58:31.716
This is… Get in.

58:32.717 --> 58:35.053
-I'll tell you about the first-aid kits.
-Okay.

58:35.136 --> 58:36.763
The smallest bag is the vitals bag.

58:36.846 --> 58:39.057
-Vitals.
-The biggest one is for wounds.

58:39.140 --> 58:40.725
This is the cardiac arrest bag.

58:40.808 --> 58:42.143
This is the fluids bag.

58:42.227 --> 58:44.687
I'll take each one out
and explain them to you.

58:44.771 --> 58:48.733
Emergency dispatch.
15-3 Boun-dong, Seongbuk-gu.

58:48.816 --> 58:50.235
-Seat belts on.
-My helmet.

59:04.624 --> 59:06.876
Wow! It's seasoned bracken!

59:11.589 --> 59:12.507
Wow!

59:24.769 --> 59:27.105
It looks so good.

59:31.067 --> 59:31.901
It's so good.

59:54.757 --> 59:55.842
Eat.

59:57.302 --> 59:58.428
What about you?

59:58.511 --> 59:59.762
I have to go right now.

01:00:04.058 --> 01:00:05.977
-What?
-I said, "Thanks."

01:00:44.182 --> 01:00:46.643
Your son's grown, and time has passed.

01:00:46.726 --> 01:00:48.227
It's time.

01:00:49.437 --> 01:00:54.067
It's an important life decision.
Think about my offer.

01:00:59.197 --> 01:01:01.783
-We're paramedics. We received a call.
-Over here!

01:01:03.409 --> 01:01:04.327
Are you okay, sir?

01:01:07.246 --> 01:01:09.832
I think I hurt my back. I can't move.

01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:12.835
We were trimming trees and I fell.

01:01:12.919 --> 01:01:14.962
There must've been a beehive here.

01:01:15.046 --> 01:01:16.881
Should I get the protective gear?

01:01:16.964 --> 01:01:18.383
No, we can't waste any more time.

01:01:18.466 --> 01:01:19.926
His condition could worsen.

01:01:20.009 --> 01:01:22.637
They're not wasps. You won't die.

01:01:22.720 --> 01:01:23.805
Come over here now.

01:01:25.556 --> 01:01:27.225
Sir, don't move.

01:01:35.149 --> 01:01:37.485
I'm glad the patient's condition
isn't serious.

01:01:38.820 --> 01:01:39.862
Yeah.

01:01:40.988 --> 01:01:46.911
But I can't really say
the same for your face.

01:01:48.496 --> 01:01:50.957
It doesn't hurt at all. I feel fine.

01:01:51.040 --> 01:01:55.002
Yeah, well… you could've just left
if things seemed dangerous.

01:01:55.086 --> 01:01:57.088
Why did you keep helping?

01:01:57.171 --> 01:01:59.465
How could I? We're a team today.

01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:00.383
United as one.

01:02:00.466 --> 01:02:01.968
United as one, my foot.

01:02:02.051 --> 01:02:04.429
Hurry and get treated.
We have to get back.

01:02:04.512 --> 01:02:07.348
No, I'm going to complete
the rest of the shift with you.

01:02:07.974 --> 01:02:11.686
How are you going to
save anyone looking like that?

01:02:11.769 --> 01:02:13.646
You should speak for yourself, Mo-eum.

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:16.274
Your face may be fine,
but you were stung all over.

01:02:16.357 --> 01:02:17.692
Why did you call me by my name?

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:22.155
Calling you "Ms. Paramedic"
seemed a bit stiff.

01:02:22.697 --> 01:02:25.116
-What should I call you then?
-Ms. Jung.

01:02:25.199 --> 01:02:26.701
We got a call from Gongsin-dong.

01:02:26.784 --> 01:02:29.370
It'd be faster to go straight there
than from the station.

01:02:29.454 --> 01:02:30.830
-Let's go.
-Okay.

01:02:33.624 --> 01:02:34.542
Let's go.

01:02:35.126 --> 01:02:36.169
Yes, Captain Jung!

01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:51.934
The patient has a herniated disk,
but there's no elevator.

01:02:52.018 --> 01:02:54.395
But we have legs.

01:02:54.479 --> 01:02:56.189
-Let's go quickly.
-Let's go.

01:03:03.696 --> 01:03:04.530
This way.

01:03:07.241 --> 01:03:08.534
Sir?

01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:13.664
You can't move, can you?

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:14.624
No.

01:03:15.833 --> 01:03:17.418
Can you help us?

01:03:18.628 --> 01:03:19.837
Lift it more, Mr. Kang.

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:20.797
Okay!

01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:22.590
Slowly.

01:03:24.050 --> 01:03:25.259
We're paramedics. Excuse us.

01:03:25.343 --> 01:03:26.677
-Did you call it in?
-Yes.

01:03:26.761 --> 01:03:27.637
What did he eat?

01:03:27.720 --> 01:03:29.639
Shrimp. He didn't say he was allergic.

01:03:30.431 --> 01:03:32.350
-Take out the oxygen tank, Mr. Kang.
-Okay.

01:03:33.518 --> 01:03:35.019
-Give me that first.
-Okay.

01:03:35.812 --> 01:03:37.522
Just a moment, sir.

01:03:41.025 --> 01:03:42.485
-I'll check his pulse.
-Okay.

01:03:43.486 --> 01:03:47.240
Doctor, the patient seems
to have gone into anaphylaxis.

01:03:47.323 --> 01:03:48.157
Yes.

01:03:48.241 --> 01:03:50.576
I'll inject him
with epinephrine and saline.

01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:52.453
-Give me the EpiPen.
-Okay.

01:03:55.122 --> 01:03:57.333
Sir, I'll administer the injection.

01:03:58.417 --> 01:03:59.836
-Hold his arm.
-Okay.

01:04:06.008 --> 01:04:08.553
Roll up his left sleeve.

01:04:10.471 --> 01:04:12.723
Can you see any veins?

01:04:18.312 --> 01:04:20.106
When I contacted you,

01:04:20.189 --> 01:04:23.192
I didn't think you'd do
this remodeling project.

01:04:23.901 --> 01:04:27.113
These days,
those boundaries are disappearing.

01:04:27.738 --> 01:04:30.491
Not to mention, I think it'll be fun.

01:04:30.575 --> 01:04:32.451
A theater is such an exciting place.

01:04:35.288 --> 01:04:36.956
I want to amplify that excitement

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:40.126
and turn it into a space where people
can experience a variety of things.

01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:41.794
We're so grateful.

01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:45.339
But it seems your affinity
for theaters is as great as ours.

01:04:46.007 --> 01:04:48.092
I have a lot of memories from theaters.

01:04:48.175 --> 01:04:49.343
You do?

01:04:49.427 --> 01:04:53.306
Yes, the first movie I ever saw
at a movie theater was Toy Story.

01:04:53.389 --> 01:04:57.226
Did you watch it with your parents
when you were a kid?

01:04:57.310 --> 01:05:00.438
No, with a friend I really liked.

01:05:11.073 --> 01:05:13.618
Since I'm here,
I'd like to see the employee area inside.

01:05:13.701 --> 01:05:15.870
-Is that possible?
-Sure, of course.

01:05:15.953 --> 01:05:17.121
Let's go.

01:05:20.666 --> 01:05:23.586
I'm on my way back to the office.
Are you coming to practice later?

01:05:23.669 --> 01:05:26.881
Hey. Can I really go?

01:05:26.964 --> 01:05:29.717
No one will be there,
and I already told Myeong-u.

01:05:29.800 --> 01:05:31.177
Okay, I'll come.

01:05:31.260 --> 01:05:32.470
See you later.

01:05:59.455 --> 01:06:00.581
What's going on?

01:06:00.665 --> 01:06:02.416
Why did you come with him?

01:06:02.500 --> 01:06:04.669
What happened was…

01:06:04.752 --> 01:06:07.630
I waited in front of her cooking class
and we came together.

01:06:08.422 --> 01:06:09.382
Look.

01:06:09.882 --> 01:06:11.884
Don't you know this is stalking?

01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:15.221
Do I have to call the cops
for you to come to your senses?

01:06:15.304 --> 01:06:17.056
I didn't follow Seok-ryu here.

01:06:17.139 --> 01:06:19.642
I heard this was an architecture firm.

01:06:20.142 --> 01:06:21.143
I came for a consult.

01:06:22.144 --> 01:06:27.400
Goodness, Seok-ryu and Mr. Choi
have brought our new client here.

01:06:28.859 --> 01:06:31.237
Please come in.
We'll serve you with love and care.

01:06:31.320 --> 01:06:32.488
What's going on?

01:06:44.333 --> 01:06:46.502
What is he here to talk about?

01:06:49.088 --> 01:06:51.090
I didn't eat anything, but I feel sick.

01:06:51.799 --> 01:06:55.094
So you want to build a house.

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.387
Yes.

01:06:56.470 --> 01:06:58.889
My parents just retired,

01:06:58.973 --> 01:07:01.392
and they're thinking
of returning to Korea.

01:07:01.475 --> 01:07:03.561
We have some land in Gapyeong.

01:07:04.353 --> 01:07:08.190
They said it'd be nice to have a house
they could use like a vacation home.

01:07:08.274 --> 01:07:13.029
That sounds nice.
What a beautiful idea, right?

01:07:13.612 --> 01:07:14.905
We at Atelier In

01:07:14.989 --> 01:07:18.659
want to give your parents the gift
of a peaceful and content retirement.

01:07:18.743 --> 01:07:22.621
Did you have a budget
or construction timeline in mind?

01:07:22.705 --> 01:07:24.623
For now…

01:07:24.707 --> 01:07:27.710
I'm aiming for next year.

01:07:27.793 --> 01:07:29.420
Just a moment. Sorry about that.

01:07:30.921 --> 01:07:32.089
Hey, Hye-ran.

01:07:33.340 --> 01:07:36.719
There's a cockroach? Just kill it.

01:07:37.344 --> 01:07:38.471
What?

01:07:38.554 --> 01:07:41.515
Okay, I'll be right there.

01:07:43.100 --> 01:07:44.560
Did something happen at home?

01:07:44.643 --> 01:07:47.772
I think Ro-hui ingested
some roach insecticide.

01:07:47.855 --> 01:07:50.107
What? Isn't that serious?

01:07:50.191 --> 01:07:51.650
The kids are doing just fine.

01:07:51.734 --> 01:07:53.569
But I think I have to go.

01:07:53.652 --> 01:07:58.032
I'm sorry.
You can finish the consult with Mr. Choi.

01:07:58.115 --> 01:07:59.575
Okay, you should go.

01:07:59.658 --> 01:08:01.869
-Yes. I have to go.
-Myeong-u, call me later.

01:08:01.952 --> 01:08:02.787
Yeah, I will.

01:08:02.870 --> 01:08:04.163
I'm sorry.

01:08:18.302 --> 01:08:19.345
Mr. Song Hyeon-jun.

01:08:21.347 --> 01:08:22.973
This consult's an excuse, isn't it?

01:08:23.057 --> 01:08:24.975
More of a justification.

01:08:25.059 --> 01:08:26.602
The plans for my parents are true.

01:08:26.685 --> 01:08:27.686
I see.

01:08:28.312 --> 01:08:30.397
But unfortunately,

01:08:30.481 --> 01:08:32.733
I have no intention of taking this on.

01:08:32.817 --> 01:08:33.859
I see.

01:08:34.819 --> 01:08:35.820
That's too bad.

01:08:36.570 --> 01:08:38.781
I heard you were a skilled architect.

01:08:38.864 --> 01:08:40.491
Of course, Seok-ryu told me.

01:08:43.536 --> 01:08:45.454
Don't say her name anymore.

01:08:46.413 --> 01:08:48.582
Don't keep showing up either.

01:08:48.666 --> 01:08:51.460
It's already over between you two.

01:08:51.544 --> 01:08:53.921
No, it's not.

01:08:54.588 --> 01:08:57.925
Our relationship is too strong
to break up that easily.

01:08:58.008 --> 01:09:00.052
That's solely what you think.

01:09:00.136 --> 01:09:01.846
You'll see it in time.

01:09:02.471 --> 01:09:05.641
You'll see what type
of relationship we had

01:09:06.267 --> 01:09:07.685
and what we meant to one another.

01:09:08.394 --> 01:09:10.479
I'm not curious about what's in the past.

01:09:11.355 --> 01:09:13.190
I only believe what Seok-ryu says.

01:09:13.941 --> 01:09:18.154
Is that belief purely based on friendship?

01:09:21.657 --> 01:09:22.491
Of course not.

01:09:30.416 --> 01:09:31.834
How's the practice going?

01:09:32.585 --> 01:09:34.128
Sorry for the wait.

01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:38.340
-Why did you follow me? Aren't you going?
-Nope. I'm going to go with Seok-ryu.

01:09:39.216 --> 01:09:40.342
If you keep this up,

01:09:40.426 --> 01:09:42.720
I'll have to report you for trespassing
and squatting.

01:09:42.803 --> 01:09:45.264
Are you arguing about jurisprudence
in front of a lawyer?

01:09:45.347 --> 01:09:47.558
Did you forget this was my firm?

01:09:47.641 --> 01:09:50.269
I'm sorry, but can you both leave?

01:09:50.352 --> 01:09:51.854
You're really disrupting my cooking.

01:09:51.937 --> 01:09:54.565
-I'll be quiet.
-I'll just watch from here.

01:10:00.946 --> 01:10:04.033
If you both sit down,

01:10:04.116 --> 01:10:05.367
I would be so grateful.

01:10:05.451 --> 01:10:06.452
Okay.

01:10:07.036 --> 01:10:08.579
-Both of you.
-Okay.

01:10:11.040 --> 01:10:11.999
Thanks.

01:10:25.888 --> 01:10:27.264
Are you really not leaving?

01:10:28.224 --> 01:10:30.643
No, I cleared my schedule.

01:10:31.227 --> 01:10:33.938
Also, I plan to eat the food
that Seok-ryu makes.

01:10:34.897 --> 01:10:37.024
I'm asking because I'm genuinely curious.

01:10:38.359 --> 01:10:40.319
Was your personality always like this?

01:10:41.445 --> 01:10:44.323
Yeah, she liked this about me.

01:10:45.157 --> 01:10:47.201
I'm strategic and have clear purposes.

01:10:48.619 --> 01:10:50.162
How much longer do I have to wait?

01:10:50.246 --> 01:10:52.206
-Are you done yet?
-Are you hungry?

01:10:52.289 --> 01:10:55.876
I just have to fry the meatballs
and boil them in the broth.

01:10:55.960 --> 01:10:58.337
Take your time.
I'll wait for as long as it takes.

01:10:59.880 --> 01:11:00.839
Take your time.

01:11:02.633 --> 01:11:03.509
By the way,

01:11:03.592 --> 01:11:05.135
it smells so good.

01:11:06.095 --> 01:11:07.763
It smells so savory and aromatic.

01:11:10.099 --> 01:11:13.227
-It smells like it's caramelizing.
-That's not my cooking.

01:11:13.852 --> 01:11:15.521
But I smelled it earlier too.

01:11:19.525 --> 01:11:21.986
I bought this for you.

01:11:23.320 --> 01:11:25.239
It's popcorn!

01:11:25.322 --> 01:11:28.033
You said you wanted
to eat some, but I'm sorry.

01:11:28.117 --> 01:11:29.034
It's cold now.

01:11:29.118 --> 01:11:30.869
It's fine. I was hungry.

01:11:30.953 --> 01:11:32.121
Don't eat that.

01:11:32.204 --> 01:11:33.664
You can't eat bad stuff like this.

01:11:33.747 --> 01:11:35.249
What are you doing?

01:11:35.958 --> 01:11:37.710
You act like I poisoned it.

01:11:37.793 --> 01:11:40.587
Trans fats aren't good for you.

01:11:44.633 --> 01:11:46.135
Now, that's the taste.

01:11:46.218 --> 01:11:48.887
This devilish sweet-and-salty flavor
flows through my veins.

01:11:49.596 --> 01:11:53.017
Remember back when we watched
Toy Story together?

01:11:53.100 --> 01:11:55.019
Of course. I remember the lines.

01:11:55.102 --> 01:11:57.313
-"To infinity and beyond!"
-"To infinity and beyond!"

01:11:57.396 --> 01:11:59.023
-You remembered?
-Of course.

01:11:59.440 --> 01:12:00.774
Leave some popcorn for me.

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:09.199
Have some.

01:12:20.627 --> 01:12:21.920
Great job.

01:12:22.004 --> 01:12:23.297
Yes, you too. Goodness.

01:12:24.256 --> 01:12:25.716
-Are you okay?
-Yes.

01:12:25.799 --> 01:12:27.468
You look like you might pass out.

01:12:27.551 --> 01:12:29.636
You lied about your stamina, didn't you?

01:12:29.720 --> 01:12:32.598
That's because everyone else's stamina
is absurdly good.

01:12:34.141 --> 01:12:35.267
Goodness.

01:12:35.809 --> 01:12:37.436
What happened to your face?

01:12:37.519 --> 01:12:39.521
He was valiantly stung by bees.

01:12:40.522 --> 01:12:41.940
He worked really hard today.

01:12:42.024 --> 01:12:44.943
He didn't work that hard.
The weather was cooler today.

01:12:45.027 --> 01:12:47.071
Our underwear get soaked
in sweat in the summer.

01:12:47.154 --> 01:12:50.199
It's too bad you won't get to know
the feeling of how it dries up.

01:12:50.282 --> 01:12:52.785
Do you prefer the start, middle,
or end of summer?

01:12:52.868 --> 01:12:53.702
I'll come back.

01:12:55.496 --> 01:12:57.247
Did you have lunch?

01:12:58.415 --> 01:12:59.625
Go get changed.

01:13:00.125 --> 01:13:01.210
Let's have dinner.

01:13:02.669 --> 01:13:03.837
Yes, sir.

01:13:03.921 --> 01:13:05.589
-Let's go.
-What are we eating?

01:13:11.887 --> 01:13:13.055
You may eat now.

01:13:13.138 --> 01:13:14.765
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

01:13:20.229 --> 01:13:22.981
This place is good.
The meat is so tender too.

01:13:24.358 --> 01:13:26.819
Captain Yeon brought you
to his favorite place.

01:13:27.403 --> 01:13:29.113
It means he's accepted you.

01:13:29.196 --> 01:13:31.407
Try the garlic sauce.
It tastes much better.

01:13:31.490 --> 01:13:34.326
-Okay.
-Try it with gat-kimchi too.

01:13:34.410 --> 01:13:35.369
It's so good.

01:13:35.452 --> 01:13:37.496
I'll pass on the honey.

01:13:37.579 --> 01:13:39.248
I have a grudge against bees now.

01:13:40.290 --> 01:13:43.585
I guess we'll get a proper article.
You saw how we had no time to eat.

01:13:43.669 --> 01:13:46.672
It's not just that.
There was no time to go to the bathroom.

01:13:46.755 --> 01:13:49.341
That's what causes
our occupational disease.

01:13:49.425 --> 01:13:50.384
Bladder infections.

01:13:50.467 --> 01:13:53.303
Captain Jung suffered from one
just last month--

01:13:53.387 --> 01:13:54.972
Hey!

01:13:55.055 --> 01:13:55.973
Eat this.

01:13:56.056 --> 01:13:57.349
I was already eating.

01:13:59.560 --> 01:14:01.019
Are there any other difficulties?

01:14:01.103 --> 01:14:02.813
Take this chance to speak freely.

01:14:05.232 --> 01:14:07.443
We don't listen to classical music.
You heard it, right?

01:14:07.526 --> 01:14:09.027
It played as our alert system.

01:14:09.111 --> 01:14:09.945
Right.

01:14:10.028 --> 01:14:12.698
Alarms would startle everyone.

01:14:12.781 --> 01:14:16.618
They changed it for our mental health.
But classical music startles us now.

01:14:17.494 --> 01:14:20.539
Once, I was on a toilet
in the bathroom of a bookstore,

01:14:20.622 --> 01:14:22.708
and I was startled to hear music
for cardiac arrest.

01:14:22.791 --> 01:14:24.960
I forgot my pants were down
and almost left.

01:14:25.627 --> 01:14:26.503
Mozart.

01:14:26.587 --> 01:14:28.213
-It's Mozart?
-Yeah.

01:14:28.297 --> 01:14:31.341
So that's why arrhythmia
is one of our occupational diseases.

01:14:31.425 --> 01:14:33.177
Because we're always stressed.

01:14:33.844 --> 01:14:35.596
How do you relieve that stress?

01:14:36.388 --> 01:14:37.473
Dating.

01:14:37.556 --> 01:14:40.309
That's what I'd like to say.
It's more of a wish.

01:14:40.392 --> 01:14:41.477
I'm single right now.

01:14:41.560 --> 01:14:43.353
Do you have time to date?

01:14:43.437 --> 01:14:44.813
We make time.

01:14:45.397 --> 01:14:49.234
Since we spend so much time together,
we end up dating each other.

01:14:49.318 --> 01:14:50.986
Workplace romances?

01:14:51.653 --> 01:14:55.324
-Have you all experienced that?
-I married my workplace romance.

01:14:55.407 --> 01:14:57.075
He dated a girl while in academy.

01:14:59.495 --> 01:15:00.537
What about you?

01:15:01.288 --> 01:15:02.372
What?

01:15:02.456 --> 01:15:04.041
I'm not interested in that.

01:15:06.126 --> 01:15:09.546
Ms. Jung likes Marvel and DC superheroes.

01:15:09.630 --> 01:15:12.257
I've never seen her impressed
with a real man before.

01:15:13.383 --> 01:15:15.802
No! There is one! Back then!

01:15:15.886 --> 01:15:17.554
The man who cleared the road.

01:15:17.638 --> 01:15:19.431
-Mudflat Man?
-Yeah, Mudflat Man.

01:15:19.515 --> 01:15:21.975
I should've looked at his plates.

01:15:22.726 --> 01:15:26.813
If you want to break down her wall,
you need to make an impact like him--

01:15:26.897 --> 01:15:28.774
Meat tastes the best when it's hot!

01:15:28.857 --> 01:15:29.691
It's hot!

01:15:29.775 --> 01:15:32.444
You're taking such good care
of him tonight.

01:15:32.528 --> 01:15:33.570
I want one too.

01:15:39.493 --> 01:15:40.661
Thank you.

01:15:41.245 --> 01:15:42.329
Let's drink.

01:15:55.175 --> 01:15:56.468
Here.

01:15:57.052 --> 01:15:58.595
Why are there two bowls?

01:15:59.429 --> 01:16:03.141
-Are you really giving him one?
-The more taste testers, the better.

01:16:03.225 --> 01:16:04.601
Evaluate it objectively.

01:16:06.144 --> 01:16:08.313
You'll understand
even if we criticize it, right?

01:16:09.022 --> 01:16:11.275
It's a necessary process for growth.

01:16:11.358 --> 01:16:13.902
You're putting a lot of significance

01:16:14.486 --> 01:16:16.405
into tasting the food, aren't you?

01:16:16.488 --> 01:16:20.117
We had an ideal relationship
where we always helped each other grow.

01:16:20.200 --> 01:16:21.368
-Sure.
-Don't eat it.

01:16:21.451 --> 01:16:23.829
-Thank you for the meal.
-Thank you for the meal.

01:16:32.379 --> 01:16:33.505
It's good.

01:16:39.094 --> 01:16:41.054
-Seok-ryu, are you okay?
-Hey, Seok-ryu!

01:16:41.138 --> 01:16:43.932
-What's wrong? Are you sick?
-My stomach…

01:16:44.433 --> 01:16:45.809
Where and how does it hurt?

01:16:46.685 --> 01:16:49.271
What are your symptoms? Can you get up?

01:16:51.231 --> 01:16:53.442
This won't do. Let's go to the hospital.

01:16:53.525 --> 01:16:54.818
I'll take you.

01:16:59.698 --> 01:17:02.034
Hyeon-jun, hold me up.

01:17:02.117 --> 01:17:03.452
You can lean on me.

01:17:26.725 --> 01:17:29.269
Miss, does your stomach hurt a lot?

01:17:29.770 --> 01:17:30.812
When did it start to hurt?

01:17:30.896 --> 01:17:32.731
Can you describe your symptoms?

01:17:33.857 --> 01:17:34.900
Three years ago…

01:17:35.901 --> 01:17:37.903
I received surgery in the US.

01:17:47.287 --> 01:17:48.914
Just a moment.

01:17:48.997 --> 01:17:52.000
These are Bae Seok-ryu's medical records.

01:17:52.084 --> 01:17:53.669
Please give them to her doctor.

01:17:54.836 --> 01:17:56.171
What kind of surgery?

01:17:57.506 --> 01:17:58.548
It was for stomach cancer.

01:17:59.841 --> 01:18:01.301
I was diagnosed with stage 2 cancer.

01:18:02.302 --> 01:18:04.304
They removed 70% of my stomach.

01:18:05.555 --> 01:18:07.140
I underwent chemotherapy.

01:18:36.086 --> 01:18:39.381
HIS SECRET

01:18:39.464 --> 01:18:44.010
HER SECRET

01:19:16.835 --> 01:19:21.047
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:19:21.131 --> 01:19:24.217
To me, Seok-ryu isn't some child.
She's a woman.

01:19:24.301 --> 01:19:27.220
How are you feeling right now?

01:19:27.304 --> 01:19:29.806
There's a gap
between Seok-ryu and me.

01:19:29.890 --> 01:19:31.057
And Hyeon-jun

01:19:31.683 --> 01:19:34.770
is inside of it
with a part of her I don't know.

01:19:34.853 --> 01:19:36.646
If you're going to start this,

01:19:36.730 --> 01:19:39.024
I want you to take
a proper path so you won't fail.

01:19:39.107 --> 01:19:41.359
Hyeon-jun proposed to me.

01:19:41.902 --> 01:19:45.822
How could you not tell me about this?

01:19:46.448 --> 01:19:48.617
This is how little I meant to you?

01:19:49.284 --> 01:19:51.077
Even as a friend,
I meant this little to you?

01:19:54.581 --> 01:19:57.584
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
